{
  "dom_id": "step-q95049",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The duration (in seconds) of the songs recorded by a music company is normally distributed with a mean of $230\\,\\text{s}$ and a standard deviation of $40\\,\\text{s}.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected song recorded by this company has a duration less than or equal to $180\\,\\text{s}?$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0901\\,$ | $\\,0.0885\\,$ | $\\,0.0869\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1075\\,$ | $\\,0.1056\\,$ | $\\,0.1038\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1271\\,$ | $\\,0.1251\\,$ | $\\,0.1230\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the duration (in seconds) of the selected song. Then we have $X∼N(230,{40}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(X<180).$ First, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<180) & =P(Z\\le \\frac{180-230}{40}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -1.25) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.25)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.25)=0.1056≈0.11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected song recorded by this company has a duration less than or equal to $180\\,\\text{s}$ is approximately $0.11.$",
